From 80af0ed1e13f7b81694cc0a2cd5e75031802d61d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:30:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] tool_store_pins: document the sticky borrower
 decline; run_tests.sh: read-only for the store

PR #1902 review nits (t_01a1d3c717fd2634).

- scripts/tool_store_pins.py: the borrower's decline of an optional default
  is sticky like any pm/defaults.py opt-out (default_packages() reads it
  back), so a long-lived borrower root keeps skipping the package after
  the owner's store gains it, until a successful `hermes pm install NAME`
  (cmd_install's record_declined(remove=...)) or deleting the record.
  The script cannot tell its own decline from the user's, so it never
  clears it. "Read-only" now says "for STORE".
- scripts/run_tests.sh: _store_has_pins is read-only for the store, not
  read-only: it can write the borrower's decline record.

Docs/comments only.
---
 scripts/run_tests.sh       |  5 +++--
 scripts/tool_store_pins.py | 11 +++++++++--
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/run_tests.sh b/scripts/run_tests.sh
index 2bddd82a04..de53de1152 100755
--- a/scripts/run_tests.sh
+++ b/scripts/run_tests.sh
@@ -89,8 +89,9 @@ _account_tool_store() {
   py_minor="$(_store_has_pins "$account/.hermes/tools")" || return 1
   printf '%s\n%s\n' "$account" "$py_minor"
 }
-# Read-only check that the store already records this checkout's pins
-# (scripts/tool_store_pins.py says why and what counts); prints the Python minor.
+# Check, read-only for the store, that it already records this checkout's pins
+# (scripts/tool_store_pins.py says why and what counts, and the one write: the
+# borrower's own decline record); prints the Python minor.
 _store_has_pins() {
   local python
   python="$(HERMES_RUNTIME_DIR="$1" hermes_bootstrap_python "$REPO_ROOT")" || return 1
diff --git a/scripts/tool_store_pins.py b/scripts/tool_store_pins.py
index c10dc001cd..0d9114db0b 100644
--- a/scripts/tool_store_pins.py
+++ b/scripts/tool_store_pins.py
@@ -19,8 +19,8 @@ without an exec-bit heal, and records the env this checkout's package code
 would record: a stale env makes `pm install` re-record the shared facts.json,
 and a missing or non-executable binary (setup-hermes.sh's uv copy included)
 sends setup or `pm install` into a re-stage whose unlocked remove + publish
-races other runs on the shared store. Read-only: no lock, no install, no
-bytecode; any unreadable record or error means "do not share".
+races other runs on the shared store. Read-only for STORE: no lock, no
+install, no bytecode; any unreadable record or error means "do not share".
 
 One exception to "every tool": an optional default (Chromium, cua-driver) the
 store records at no version at all, because the owner declined it or it failed
@@ -28,6 +28,13 @@ to install (cua-driver on a headless Linux worker lacks libXi). The borrower
 declines it too, so its own `pm install` never stages it into the shared store.
 That decline, written only once every check passed, is this script's one write,
 and it lands in the borrower's install state, never in STORE.
+
+The decline is sticky, like any opt-out in pm/defaults.py: later runs read it
+back through default_packages(), so the package is neither checked nor staged
+again, even after the owner's store gains it. A long-lived borrower root keeps
+skipping it until a successful `hermes pm install NAME` (the opt-back-in,
+which clears the record) or deleting <root>/installs/<key>/declined-packages.json.
+This script never clears it: it cannot tell its own decline from the user's.
 """
 import os
 import sys
-- 
